# Elias — Friday, 6:50am, Kitchen, Ferndale Road

**What I do:** Before the radiator job, before the van even warms up, I thumb two texts to Mare. Not tonight — now, while the ink's still wet on ASK FIRST.

> "Up. Two things before I forget them. 1) Callum texted 11:15 last night — 'sorted the van thing, bit tight this side of xmas.' No amount, no date. Haven't replied. You hear it from me, second time running. 2) The Ferndale Fund standing order — £250, fires Monday, and the fund's empty because I emptied it. I forgot it existed. What do we do — pause it, feed it, kill it? Your call as much as mine. — E"

That's the difference she asked for. I decided alone twice; there won't be a third [33b996b050d9].

At Mossley Rise, bleeding the radiator, I ring her back on speaker:

> "Sunday. Frost means every boiler in town dies by nine — I could earn a week's takings. And I'd rather be at Mum's table watching Callum squirm. So: I work till noon, arrive late but arrive, and I tell Mum today that's the deal. Unless you'd rather I not come at all — say it, I'll take it."

Then Callum gets his answer, terms attached, because Mare's had hers first:

> "Van thing's settled, ta. Money: send £200 by Christmas or say you can't — either's fine, silence isn't. And you'll be civil to Mare Sunday or stay home."

**How I feel:**
- **Fear/anxiety — 6/10.** Down from 8. The texts are sent; dread shrinks when it's spoken.
- **Rejection/hurt — 4/10.** Her kiss ran half a second long. Half a second is not nothing.
- **Affection — 7/10.** Still climbing off yesterday's six [3c2cb0073c5b, 08b459b233c0] — the gap between log and life keeps closing.
- **Anger — 3/10.** Absent in every replay I've got [2b4fcb370cd6, ef1458190cf7], but "legend" with no amount stirs it. At him, not her.
- **Disgust — 2/10.** At myself: I forgot my own standing order [f22b404402c3].
- **Sadness — 5/10.** Below the eleven-day floor of 6.
- **Happiness — 4/10.** Leeds stays HELD. Nothing fought over.
- **Surprise — 1/10.** Callum texting at all.

Repair wins again, four seeds in five [2c42e1f47e8d, 09d3999016fc, 5fcbab072563, 33b996b050d9]. One untold thing left. Dad waits.
